  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Working of an NPN transistor"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "The emitter–base junction is forward biased, so electrons are injected from the emitter into the base. The base is thin and lightly doped, so only a few electrons (about 1–5%) recombine with holes there, forming the small base current. The rest diffuse to the collector–base junction, which is reverse biased; its field sweeps them into the collector, forming the collector current."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "E–B junction forward biased, C–B junction reverse biased"
    },
    {
     "en": "Most injected electrons reach the collector"
    },
    {
     "en": "Recombination in the base gives the small I_B"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "The forward-biased emitter junction injects electrons into the thin base. Only a few recombine; most are swept into the collector by the reverse-biased collector junction.",
    "kn": "ಮುಂದುಮುಖ ಬಯಾಸ್‌ನ ಎಮಿಟರ್ ಸಂಧಿ ತೆಳುವಾದ ಬೇಸ್‌ಗೆ ಎಲೆಕ್ಟ್ರಾನ್‌ಗಳನ್ನು ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತದೆ. ಕೆಲವೇ ಎಲೆಕ್ಟ್ರಾನ್‌ಗಳು ಮರುಸಂಯೋಜನೆಯಾಗುತ್ತವೆ; ಉಳಿದವು ಹಿಮ್ಮುಖ ಬಯಾಸ್‌ನ ಕಲೆಕ್ಟರ್ ಸಂಧಿಯಿಂದ ಕಲೆಕ್ಟರ್‌ಗೆ ಸೆಳೆಯಲ್ಪಡುತ್ತವೆ."
   }
  },
